.direnv/
target/
result
result-*
# ⚠️ ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. A bare `runtime/` matches at ANY depth, so it also caught
# faelight/engine/src/runtime/ -- a SOURCE directory. The file inside stayed tracked because it
# predated the rule, which is why nothing complained until the formatting hook tried to re-stage it
# and could not, blocking every commit that touched it (2026-08-26).
# The state directory this was written for lives outside the repo now; the leading slash keeps the
# intent for the repo root without swallowing source.
/runtime/
faelight-vm.qcow2
*.bak-*

# INT-119: generated by git-hooks.nix from flake.nix on devShell entry. Not source.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
__pycache__/
faelight/runtime/legacy-exec.log
faelight/runtime/sh-fallback.log
/0.5
/=

# ship writes a copy of each outgoing binary here before replacing it, so
# core deploy rollback has something to restore. Machine-local state, not
# source: regenerated on every ship, ~25MB, and meaningless on another
# machine. Anchored for the same reason /runtime/ is -- a bare bin/ would
# match at any depth and swallow a source directory named bin.
/bin/
